Description: Fix configure test programs that clang 16 and newer (FreeBSD 14/15 base: clang 19) and gcc 14 and newer reject for their implicit int return type, so they failed silently: whether write(2) to stdout works (the CLI then wrote through stdio instead of write(2)), the run check of PHP_CHECK_FUNC_LIB (functions found only in a separate library) and the reentrant time function type. The sources need no change for those compilers.
Origin: azsupport; configure results checked against a run with those errors turned into warnings: identical main/php_config.h

diff --git a/build/php.m4 b/build/php.m4
index 86b522a39..5f2206e89 100644
--- a/build/php.m4
+++ b/build/php.m4
@@ -1120,7 +1120,7 @@ AC_CACHE_CHECK(for type of reentrant time-related functions, ac_cv_time_r_type,[
 AC_RUN_IFELSE([AC_LANG_SOURCE([[
 #include <time.h>
 
-main() {
+int main() {
 char buf[27];
 struct tm t;
 time_t old = 0;
@@ -1136,7 +1136,7 @@ return (1);
 ],[
   AC_RUN_IFELSE([AC_LANG_SOURCE([[
 #include <time.h>
-main() {
+int main() {
   struct tm t, *s;
   time_t old = 0;
   char buf[27], *p;
@@ -1597,7 +1597,7 @@ AC_DEFUN([PHP_CHECK_FUNC_LIB],[
   if test "$found" = "yes"; then
     ac_libs=$LIBS
     LIBS="$LIBS -l$2"
-    AC_RUN_IFELSE([AC_LANG_SOURCE([[main() { return (0); }]])],[found=yes],[found=no],[found=no])
+    AC_RUN_IFELSE([AC_LANG_SOURCE([[int main(void) { return (0); }]])],[found=yes],[found=no],[found=no])
     LIBS=$ac_libs
   fi
 
@@ -2285,7 +2285,7 @@ AC_DEFUN([PHP_TEST_WRITE_STDOUT],[
 
 #define TEXT "This is the test message -- "
 
-main()
+int main()
 {
   int n;
 
